Alex wants to rent a car to travel to a destination that is N kilometers away. He has two options: 
1) Rent a petrol car. 2) Rent a diesel car.

The cost of one liter of petrol is X rupees, and the cost of one liter of diesel is Y rupees. The petrol car can travel A kilometers per
liter, while the diesel car can travel B kilometers per liter. Fuel can be purchased in fractional quantities if required. Determine which
type of car results in the lowest travel cost.

Print "PETROL" if the petrol car is cheaper. Print "DIESEL" if the diesel car is cheaper. Print "ANY" if both options cost the same.

Input Format
A single line containing five space-separated integers : N X Y A B

where: N = Distance to travel (in kilometers), X = Cost of one liter of petrol, Y = Cost of one liter of diesel, A = Mileage of petrol 
car (km/l), B = Mileage of diesel car (km/l)

Output Format
Print one of the following: PETROL or DIESEL or ANY




#include <iostream>
#include <bits/stdc++.h>
using namespace std;
int main()
{
    int N,X,Y,A,B;
    cin>>N>>X>>Y>>A>>B;
    int petrol=(N/A)*X;
    int diesel=(N/B)*Y;
    if(petrol<diesel){
        cout<<"PETROL";
    }
    else if(petrol>diesel){
        cout<<"DIESEL";
    }
    else{
        cout<<"ANY";
    }

    return 0;
}
